{"repositoryId":1188636885,"availability":"available","full":"zymbol-lang/interpreter","name":"interpreter","description":"Zymbol-Lang interpreter — symbolic programming language, no keywords, full Unicode, dual execution (tree-walker + register VM)","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":5,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-22T11:23:45Z","updated":"2026-10-12T18:50:19Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://zymbol-lang.org/playground.html","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:51.039Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:51.039Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:51.039Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:51.039Z","stars":5,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A minimalist symbolic programming language with no words in its grammar.","Pure symbols for every construct. Full Unicode. Built in Rust.","Zymbol started as an esoteric programming language — a single tight question taken seriously: what happens if you remove every word? No if, no while, no function, no return. The original experiment is on esolangs.org. Then the idea grew."],"features":["No words — pure symbolic syntax (? if, @ loop, >> output, -> lambda). Not","\"no keywords\": keyword is a tokenizer's term for a reserved token, and by that reading the language server files ? and @ under KEYWORD because LSP has no other slot. The checkable claim is that no construct of the…","Dual execution — tree-walker interpreter and register-based VM (--vm)","Full Unicode — identifiers, strings, and numerals support any Unicode script","First-class functions — named functions as values, HOF arguments, and closures"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zymbol-lang/interpreter/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5bf3058d4fd851bdef92289729aa9d200aefba90cfe37eee7972a695eea25dba","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:51.160Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:51.160Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,